# Frontend/.dockerignore

# ==========================================================================
# === SECTION 1: DEPENDENCIES & PACKAGE MANAGERS ===
# ==========================================================================
# WHY THIS FIX IS NECESSARY: Prevents transferring host operating system binaries 
# into the Docker container. Dependencies must be installed inside the container environment.
node_modules
.npm
.yarn
.pnpm-store
# === SECTION 1 END ===

# ==========================================================================
# === SECTION 2: SECURITY & ENVIRONMENT SECRETS ===
# ==========================================================================
# WHY THIS FIX IS NECESSARY: Catch-all wildcard pattern ensures NO environment file 
# containing API keys, database credentials, or secret tokens can leak into build artifacts.
.env
.env*
!.env.example

# WHY THIS FIX IS NECESSARY: Blocks private cryptographic keys and auth configurations 
# from being bundled into container image layers.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
.npmrc
.yarnrc
# === SECTION 2 END ===

# ==========================================================================
# === SECTION 3: FRAMEWORK BUILD OUTPUTS & CACHES ===
# ==========================================================================
# WHY THIS FIX IS NECESSARY: Prevents stale host build outputs from interfering with 
# fresh multi-stage Next.js production builds inside the container.
.next
out
build
dist
.cache
coverage
# === SECTION 3 END ===

# ==========================================================================
# === SECTION 4: VERSION CONTROL & SYSTEM JUNK ===
# ==========================================================================
# WHY THIS FIX IS NECESSARY: Speeds up Docker build context evaluation by omitting 
# git history, OS files, and developer documentation.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode
.idea
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
README.md
# === SECTION 4 END ===